      <h2 id="cluster-api-sample-yaml-bare-metal_cluster-api-config-options-bare-metal" class="group scroll-mt-20">Sample YAML for configuring bare metal clusters<a href="#cluster-api-sample-yaml-bare-metal_cluster-api-config-options-bare-metal" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>The following example YAML files show configurations for a bare metal cluster.</p>
      <h3 id="capi-yaml-machine-template-bare-metal_cluster-api-config-options-bare-metal" class="group scroll-mt-20">Sample YAML for a Cluster API machine template resource on bare metal<a href="#capi-yaml-machine-template-bare-metal_cluster-api-config-options-bare-metal" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p class="_abstract">The machine template resource is provider-specific and defines the basic properties of the machines that a compute machine set creates. The compute machine set references this template when creating machines.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: infrastructure.cluster.x-k8s.io/v1beta1\nkind: Metal3MachineTemplate\nmetadata:\n  name: <template_name>\n  namespace: openshift-cluster-api\nspec:\n  template:\n    spec:\n      customDeploy: install_coreos\n      userData: \n        name: worker-user-data-managed"} lang="yaml" />
